-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, 1992 c. 4 -- part ssc5.
-- PART IX, CHILD BENEFIT (ss 141 to 147).  Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk (point in time
-- 2026-07-08); it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- Reading a result: JUST FALSE is the Act saying no in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md).
-- Every NOT is bracketed.  Day of the week: Day (a date) MODULO 7 is 0 for Sunday, 1 for Monday ... 6 for Saturday.
-- Child benefit's grant (s 141) and its flat negatives (ss 144(3), 146, Schedule 9) are in different places;
-- `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` puts them together.

§ `Part IX -- Child benefit (ss 141-147)`

§§ `s 142 -- "child" and "qualifying young person"`

-- A person is a child if he has not attained 16.  "Has not attained" is s 173(a)'s "under" (a seam, K2).
-- src:2927 | (1) For the purposes of this Part of this Act a person is a child if he has not attained the age of 16.
@ref s 142(1) (src:2927)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person is under 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142(1) the person is a child` MEANS
    `s 173(a) the person is under 16`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words), via s 173(a)'s JUST FALSE: "a person is a child if he has not attained the age of 16"

-- A qualifying young person is a person, other than a child, who has not attained the age the Treasury
-- prescribes (greater than 16) and who satisfies the conditions so prescribed.
-- src:2928 | (2) In this Part of this Act “qualifying young person” means a person, other than a child, who —
-- src:2929 | (a) has not attained such age (greater than 16) as is prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury, and
-- src:2930 | (b) satisfies conditions so prescribed.
@ref s 142(2) (src:2928-2930)
GIVEN `s 142(1) the person is a child` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the person is under the age prescribed under subsection (2)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person satisfies the conditions prescribed under subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142(2) the person is a qualifying young person` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualifying young person” means a person, other than a child, who" -- when a limb fails, JUST FALSE
    `s 124(1) all of these hold` (LIST
        `s 124(1) does not hold` `s 142(1) the person is a child`
        , `s 173(a) the person is under the age prescribed under subsection (2)(a)`
        , JUST `the person satisfies the conditions prescribed under subsection (2)(b)`)

§§ `s 143 -- the person responsible for a child or qualifying young person`

DECLARE `s 143(3) Reason for the absence` IS ONE OF
    `s 143(3)(a) receiving education or training of a description prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury`
    `s 143(3)(b) undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution`
    `s 143(3)(c) in residential accommodation pursuant to arrangements made under one of the Acts listed, in prescribed circumstances`
    `s 143(3) some other reason`

-- A gloss: a day of absence is disregarded if it is due solely to education or training, in-patient treatment,
-- or residential accommodation under the listed arrangements in prescribed circumstances (and subject to
-- the limit in subsection (4)).
-- src:2936 | (3) Subject to subsection (4) below, a day of absence shall be disregarded for the purposes of subsection (2) above if it is due solely to the fact that the child or qualifying young person is—
-- src:2937 | (a) receiving education or training of a description prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury;
-- src:2938 | (b) undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution; or
-- src:2939 | (c) ... in such circumstances as may be prescribed, in residential accommodation pursuant to arrangements made under—
-- src:2940 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:2941 | (ii) the Children Act 1989;
-- src:2942 | (iii) the Social Work (Scotland) Act 1968;
-- src:2943 | (iv) the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978;
-- src:2944 | (v) the Education (Scotland) Act 1980;
-- src:2945 | (vi) the Mental Health (Scotland) Act 1984;
-- src:2946 | (vii) the Children (Scotland) Act 1995; ...
-- src:2947 | (viii) the Children’s Hearings (Scotland) Act 2011 or
-- src:2948 | (ix) Part 4 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014.
@ref s 143(3) (src:2936-2948)
GIVEN reason IS A `s 143(3) Reason for the absence`
      `the absence is due solely to that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for reason (c), the circumstances are prescribed ones` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143(3) the day of absence is disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the absence is due solely to that fact`
    THEN
        CONSIDER reason
        WHEN `s 143(3)(a) receiving education or training of a description prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 143(3)(b) undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 143(3)(c) in residential accommodation pursuant to arrangements made under one of the Acts listed, in prescribed circumstances` THEN
            IF `for reason (c), the circumstances are prescribed ones` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in such circumstances as may be prescribed"
        WHEN `s 143(3) some other reason` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (3) lists three reasons and does not say "only"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is due solely to the fact that"

-- (4): the days disregarded under (3)(b) or (c) may not exceed the prescribed number, unless the person claiming
-- to be responsible regularly incurs expenditure in respect of the child; (3)(a) days are not limited.
-- src:2949 | (4) The number of days that may be disregarded by virtue of subsection (3)(b) or (c) above in the case of any child or qualifying young person shall not exceed such number as may be prescribed unless the person claiming to be responsible for the child or qualifying young person regularly incurs expenditure in respect of him.
@ref s 143(4) (src:2949)
GIVEN `the days disregarded under subsection (3)(a)` IS A NUMBER
      `the days disregarded under subsection (3)(b) or (c)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days prescribed` IS A NUMBER
      `the person regularly incurs expenditure in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 143(4) the number of days that may be disregarded` MEANS
    `the days disregarded under subsection (3)(a)`
    PLUS (   IF `the person regularly incurs expenditure in respect of the child or qualifying young person`
             THEN `the days disregarded under subsection (3)(b) or (c)`
             ELSE min `the days disregarded under subsection (3)(b) or (c)` `the number of days prescribed`)

-- (2): a child who lived with the person at some time before the week is treated as living with him in the
-- week despite absence, unless in the 16 weeks before it they were apart for more than 56 days, not counting
-- the days disregarded under (3).
-- src:2935 | (2) Where a person has had a child or qualifying young person living with him at some time before a particular week he shall be treated for the purposes of this section as having the child or qualifying young person living with him in that week notwithstanding their absence from one another unless, in the 16 weeks preceding that week, they were absent from one another for more than 56 days not counting any day which is to be disregarded under subsection (3) below.
@ref s 143(2) (src:2935)
GIVEN `the person has had the child or qualifying young person living with the person at some time before the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days in the 16 weeks preceding the week on which they were absent from one another` IS A NUMBER
      `the days of those to be disregarded under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week` MEANS
    IF `the person has had the child or qualifying young person living with the person at some time before the week`
    THEN
        IF (`the days in the 16 weeks preceding the week on which they were absent from one another` MINUS `the days of those to be disregarded under subsection (3)`) GREATER THAN 56
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, in the 16 weeks preceding that week, they were absent from one another for more than 56 days not counting any day which is to be disregarded under subsection (3) below"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person has had a child or qualifying young person living with him at some time before a particular week"

-- (1)(a): the person has the child living with him in the week (including by the deeming in (2)).
-- src:2933 | (a) he has the child or qualifying young person living with him in that week; or
@ref s 143(1)(a) (src:2933)
GIVEN `the child or qualifying young person is living with the person in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` MEANS
    `the child or qualifying young person is living with the person in the week`
    OR `s 124(1) is known to hold` `s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week`

-- (1)(b): the person contributes to the cost of providing for the child at a weekly rate not less than the
-- weekly rate of child benefit payable for the child for that week.
-- src:2934 | (b) he is contributing to the cost of providing for the child or qualifying young person at a weekly rate which is not less than the weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of the child or qualifying young person for that week.
@ref s 143(1)(b) (src:2934)
GIVEN `the weekly rate at which the person contributes to the cost of providing for the child or qualifying young person in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 143(1)(b) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b)` MEANS
    `the weekly rate at which the person contributes to the cost of providing for the child or qualifying young person in pounds`
        AT LEAST `the weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week in pounds`

-- src:2932 | (1) For the purposes of this Part of this Act a person shall be treated as responsible for a child or qualifying young person in any week if—
-- src:2933 | (a) he has the child or qualifying young person living with him in that week; or
-- src:2934 | (b) he is contributing to the cost of providing for the child or qualifying young person at a weekly rate which is not less than the weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of the child or qualifying young person for that week.
@ref s 143(1) (src:2932-2934)
GIVEN `s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 143(1)(b) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143(1) the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person in the week` MEANS
    IF `s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` OR `s 143(1)(b) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person shall be treated as responsible for a child or qualifying young person in any week if"

-- Contributions "over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)" (asked by s 77, Schedule 7):
-- read as contributions at a weekly rate above the weekly rate of child benefit that paragraph (b) requires
-- (fork F4 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2934 | (b) he is contributing to the cost of providing for the child or qualifying young person at a weekly rate which is not less than the weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of the child or qualifying young person for that week.
@ref s 143(1)(b) (src:2934)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the contributions in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)` MEANS
    JUST (`the weekly rate of the contributions in pounds` GREATER THAN `the weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week in pounds`)

§§ `ss 144 to 146 -- exclusions, priority, rate, death, presence`

-- (2): Schedule 9 has effect for excluding entitlement to child benefit.  Schedule 9 is another part's: its
-- answer is the input, and JUST TRUE is the text's own "excluding entitlement".
-- src:2956 | (2) Schedule 9 to this Act shall have effect for excluding entitlement to child benefit ....
@ref s 144(2) (src:2956)
GIVEN `sch 9 the exclusion from entitlement to child benefit applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(2) entitlement to child benefit is excluded by Schedule 9` MEANS
    `sch 9 the exclusion from entitlement to child benefit applies`   -- NOTHING when Schedule 9's answer is not known; a JUST FALSE is Schedule 9's, not this subsection's

-- (3): where two or more persons would be entitled for the same child and week, one of them only is entitled,
-- decided under Schedule 10 (a seam: ssc9 answers).  Fewer than two: the subsection does not arise.
-- src:2957 | (3) Where, apart from this subsection, two or more persons would be entitled to child benefit in respect of the same child or qualifying young person for the same week, one of them only shall be entitled; and the question which of them is entitled shall be determined in accordance with Schedule 10 to this Act.
@ref s 144(3) (src:2957)
GIVEN `the number of persons who would be entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week apart from this subsection` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 10 the person is the one entitled under the priority rules` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(3) the person is the one entitled among those who would be entitled` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons who would be entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week apart from this subsection` AT LEAST 2
    THEN `sch 10 the person is the one entitled under the priority rules`   -- a JUST FALSE here is the text's "one of them only shall be entitled"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where ... two or more persons would be entitled"

-- src:2959 | (1) Child benefit shall be payable at such weekly rate as may be prescribed.
@ref s 145(1) (src:2959)
GIVEN `the weekly rate prescribed for the case, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 145(1) the weekly rate of child benefit in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate prescribed for the case, if there is one`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when none is given: "such weekly rate as may be prescribed"

-- src:2962 | (4) No rate prescribed in place of a rate previously in force shall be lower than the rate that it replaces.
@ref s 145(4) (src:2962)
GIVEN `the rate prescribed in place of a rate previously in force in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate it replaces in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(4) the rate prescribed may be lower than the rate it replaces` MEANS
    IF `the rate prescribed in place of a rate previously in force in pounds` LESS THAN `the rate it replaces in pounds`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No rate prescribed in place of a rate previously in force shall be lower than the rate that it replaces."
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection forbids a lower rate; it does not say a higher or equal rate is lawful

-- src:2985 | (1) No child benefit shall be payable in respect of a child or qualifying young person for a week unless he is in Great Britain in that week.
@ref s 146(1) (src:2985)
GIVEN `the child or qualifying young person is in Great Britain in the week (or is treated as being, under regulations)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(1) the child or qualifying young person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the child or qualifying young person is in Great Britain in the week (or is treated as being, under regulations)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No child benefit shall be payable in respect of a child or qualifying young person for a week unless he is in Great Britain in that week."

-- src:2986 | (2) No person shall be entitled to child benefit for a week unless he is in Great Britain in that week.
@ref s 146(2) (src:2986)
GIVEN `the person is in Great Britain in the week (or is treated as being, under regulations)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(2) the person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the person is in Great Britain in the week (or is treated as being, under regulations)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be entitled to child benefit for a week unless he is in Great Britain in that week."

§§ `s 141 -- entitlement to child benefit`

-- A gloss: a person who is responsible for a child (or qualifying young person) in a week is entitled to
-- child benefit for that week, subject to the rest of the Part: the child and the person must be in Great
-- Britain (s 146), Schedule 9 must not exclude entitlement (s 144(2)), and where several persons would be
-- entitled only the one Schedule 10 picks is (s 144(3)).  Schedules 9 and 10 are ssc9's: their answers are
-- inputs.  A bar that the Act states is JUST FALSE; the grant itself is limited by "a person who is responsible".
-- src:2925 | A person who is responsible for one or more children or qualifying young persons in any week shall be entitled, subject to the provisions of this Part of this Act, to a benefit (to be known as “child benefit") for that week in respect of the child or qualifying young person, or each of the children or qualifying young persons, for whom he is responsible.
@ref s 141 (src:2925)
GIVEN `s 143(1) the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person in the week` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 146(1) the child or qualifying young person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 146(2) the person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 144(2) entitlement to child benefit is excluded by Schedule 9` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons who would be entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week apart from this subsection` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 10 the person is the one entitled under the priority rules` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the bars`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 146(1), s 146(2) "unless he is in Great Britain", s 144(2) "Schedule 9 ... excluding entitlement", s 144(3) "one of them only shall be entitled"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 143(1) the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person in the week`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is responsible for one or more children or qualifying young persons"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): responsibility is not known
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING          -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a bar from a Schedule or a prescribed circumstance is not known
    WHERE
        `the bars` MEANS
            `s 124(1) all of these hold` (LIST
                `s 146(1) the child or qualifying young person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires`
                , `s 146(2) the person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires`
                , `s 124(1) does not hold` `s 144(2) entitlement to child benefit is excluded by Schedule 9`
                , `the bar of subsection 144(3)`)
        `the bar of subsection 144(3)` MEANS
            -- fewer than two persons: the subsection does not arise, so nothing bars this person (a step in combining the bars, not a statement of entitlement)
            IF `the number of persons who would be entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week apart from this subsection` AT LEAST 2
            THEN `s 144(3) the person is the one entitled among those who would be entitled`
                    `the number of persons who would be entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week apart from this subsection`
                    `sch 10 the person is the one entitled under the priority rules`
            ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 145A -- entitlement after the death of a child or qualifying young person`

-- (1): a person entitled for the week in which the child or qualifying young person dies is entitled for a
-- prescribed period after that week.
-- src:2967 | (1) If a child or qualifying young person dies and a person is entitled to child benefit in respect of him for the week in which his death occurs, that person shall be entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person for a prescribed period following that week.
@ref s 145A(1) (src:2967)
GIVEN `the child or qualifying young person died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week in which the death occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the week asked about, counting the first week after the week of death as 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the length of the prescribed period in weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(1) the person is entitled to child benefit for the week after the death` MEANS
    IF     `the child or qualifying young person died`
       AND `the person was entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person for the week in which the death occurred`
       AND `the number of the week asked about, counting the first week after the week of death as 1` AT LEAST 1
       AND `the number of the week asked about, counting the first week after the week of death as 1` AT MOST `the length of the prescribed period in weeks`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a prescribed period following that week"

-- (5): married couple, civil partnership and cohabiting couple, for this section.
-- src:2979 | “married couple” means a man and a woman who are married to each other and are neither—
-- src:2980 | separated under a court order, nor
-- src:2981 | separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent, and
@ref s 145A(5) “married couple” (src:2979-2981)
GIVEN `the two people are a man and a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are married to each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are separated under a court order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(5) the two people are a married couple` MEANS
    IF     `the two people are a man and a woman` AND `they are married to each other`
       AND (NOT `they are separated under a court order`)
       AND (NOT `they are separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“married couple” means a man and a woman who are married to each other and are neither— separated under a court order, nor separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent"

-- src:2975 | “civil partnership” means two people ... who are civil partners of each other and are neither—
-- src:2976 | separated under a court order, nor
-- src:2977 | separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent;
@ref s 145A(5) “civil partnership” (src:2975-2977)
GIVEN `they are civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are separated under a court order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(5) the two people are a civil partnership` MEANS
    IF     `they are civil partners of each other`
       AND (NOT `they are separated under a court order`)
       AND (NOT `they are separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“civil partnership” means two people ... who are civil partners of each other and are neither— separated under a court order, nor separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent"

-- src:2978 | “cohabiting couple” means two people who are not married to, or civil partners, of each other but are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners;
@ref s 145A(5) “cohabiting couple” (src:2978)
GIVEN `they are married to, or civil partners of, each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(5) the two people are a cohabiting couple` MEANS
    IF (NOT `they are married to, or civil partners of, each other`) AND `they are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cohabiting couple” means two people who are not married to, or civil partners, of each other but are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners"

-- (2): if the person entitled under (1) dies before the prescribed period ends, and at death was a member of a
-- married couple or civil partnership living with the spouse or civil partner, or a member of a cohabiting
-- couple, the other member is entitled for the rest of the period.  "And living with" is an extra condition of limb
-- (a), on top of the definitions in (5) (fork F3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2968 | (2) If the person entitled to child benefit under subsection (1) dies before the end of that prescribed period and, at the time of his death, was—
-- src:2969 | (a) a member of a married couple or civil partnership and living with the person to whom he was married or who was his civil partner, or
-- src:2970 | (b) a member of a cohabiting couple,
-- src:2971 | that other member of the couple or partnership shall be entitled to child benefit for the period for which the dead person would have been entitled to child benefit under subsection (1) above but for his death.
@ref s 145A(2) (src:2968-2971)
GIVEN `the person entitled under subsection (1) died before the end of the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 145A(5) the two people are a married couple` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 145A(5) the two people are a civil partnership` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 145A(5) the two people are a cohabiting couple` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the dead person was living with the person to whom he was married or who was his civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` MEANS
    IF `the person entitled under subsection (1) died before the end of the prescribed period`
    THEN
        `s 124(1) holds or else nothing`
            (`s 124(1) either holds`
                (`s 124(1) both hold` (`s 124(1) either holds` `s 145A(5) the two people are a married couple` `s 145A(5) the two people are a civil partnership`)
                                      (JUST `the dead person was living with the person to whom he was married or who was his civil partner`))
                `s 145A(5) the two people are a cohabiting couple`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the person entitled to child benefit under subsection (1) dies before the end of that prescribed period"

-- src:2972 | (3) If a child dies before the end of the week in which he is born, subsections (1) and (2) apply in his case as if references to the person entitled to child benefit in respect of a child for the week in which his death occurs were to the person who would have been so entitled if the child had been alive at the beginning of that week (and if any conditions which were satisfied, and any facts which existed, at the time of his death were satisfied or existed then).
@ref s 145A(3) (src:2972)
GIVEN `the child died before the end of the week in which the child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(3) subsections (1) and (2) apply as if the person were the one who would have been entitled had the child been alive at the beginning of the week` MEANS
    IF `the child died before the end of the week in which the child was born`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a child dies before the end of the week in which he is born"

-- src:2973 | (4) Where a person is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person under this section, section 77 applies with the omission of subsections (4) to (6).
@ref s 145A(4) (src:2973)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to child benefit under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(4) section 77 applies with the omission of subsections (4) to (6)` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to child benefit under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person is entitled to child benefit ... under this section"

§§ `s 147 -- interpretation of Part IX`

-- "week" is 7 days beginning with a Monday.  Day (a date) MODULO 7 is 1 for Monday.
-- src:2995 | “week” means a period of 7 days beginning with a Monday.
@ref s 147(1) “week” (src:2995)
GIVEN date IS A DATE
GIVETH A Period
`s 147(1) the week containing the date` MEANS
    Period WITH
        `the first day` IS date MINUS (((Day date) PLUS 6) MODULO 7)
        `the last day`  IS (date MINUS (((Day date) PLUS 6) MODULO 7)) PLUS 6

-- src:2994 | “voluntary organisation” means a body, other than a public or local authority, the activities of which are carried on otherwise than for profit; and
@ref s 147(1) “voluntary organisation” (src:2994)
GIVEN `the body is a public or local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its activities are carried on otherwise than for profit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(1) the body is a voluntary organisation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the body is a public or local authority`) AND `its activities are carried on otherwise than for profit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voluntary organisation” means a body, other than a public or local authority, the activities of which are carried on otherwise than for profit"

DECLARE `s 147(1) Defined term` IS ONE OF
    `s 147(1) prescribed`

-- src:2992 | “prescribed” means prescribed by regulations;
@ref s 147(1) “prescribed” (src:2992)
GIVEN term IS A `s 147(1) Defined term`
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 147(1) how the term is defined` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
        `what it points at or says` IS "prescribed by regulations"

-- (2): a condition satisfied or a fact existing "in a week" is judged at the beginning of that week, subject to
-- regulations.
-- src:2996 | (2) Subject to any provision made by regulations, references in this Part of this Act to any condition being satisfied or any facts existing in a week shall be construed as references to the condition being satisfied or the facts existing at the beginning of that week.
@ref s 147(2) (src:2996)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
      `regulations provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 147(2) the day on which a condition or fact in the week is judged` MEANS
    IF `regulations provide otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any provision made by regulations"
    ELSE JUST `the first day of the week`

DECLARE `s 147(3) Relation to the child or qualifying young person` IS ONE OF
    `s 147(3) a step-parent`
    `s 147(3) a step-father`
    `s 147(3) a step-mother`
    `s 147(3) some other relation`

-- src:2997 | (3) References in this Part of this Act to a parent, father or mother of a child or qualifying young person shall be construed as including references to a step-parent, step-father or step-mother.
@ref s 147(3) (src:2997)
GIVEN relation IS A `s 147(3) Relation to the child or qualifying young person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(3) the person is within a reference in this Part to a parent, father or mother` MEANS
    CONSIDER relation
    WHEN `s 147(3) a step-parent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 147(3) a step-father` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 147(3) a step-mother` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 147(3) some other relation` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "shall be construed as including references to a step-parent, step-father or step-mother"

-- src:3000 | (6) Nothing in this Part of this Act shall be construed as conferring a right to child benefit on any body corporate; but regulations may confer such a right on voluntary organisations and for that purpose may make such modifications as the Secretary of State thinks fit—
@ref s 147(6) (src:3000)
GIVEN `the person claiming is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations confer a right to child benefit on the body as a voluntary organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(6) this Part confers a right to child benefit on the body` MEANS
    IF `the person claiming is a body corporate`
    THEN
        IF `regulations confer a right to child benefit on the body as a voluntary organisation`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "but regulations may confer such a right on voluntary organisations"
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Part of this Act shall be construed as conferring a right to child benefit on any body corporate"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a body corporate
